<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Quintus Fabius Maximus</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Fabius Maximus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Quintus Fabius Maximus was a Roman statesman and general during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-punic-war">Second Punic War</a>. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a>'s early victories he adopted a strategy of avoiding pitched battle and wearing down the Carthaginian army, earning the name Cunctator, the delayer. The strategy helped <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> survive Hannibal's invasion and contributed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punic-empire">Punic Empire</a>'s eventual defeat.</p></div>
